      "message": "Put the owner in every repository's name\n\nA repository is now named owner/name, where the owner is the person or\norganisation that holds it, and that name is its address everywhere:\nthe pages at /owner/name, git at /git/owner/name, the API at\n/api/repos/owner/name, and the directory on disk. An organisation is a\nteam that owns repositories: its members act for it, so the New form\noffers your own name and every organisation you belong to, and an owner\npage lists what an owner holds. Ownership still moves only by an\naccepted offer, and accepting now renames the repository under its new\nowner. Every former name, from a rename or a transfer, keeps answering\nwith a permanent redirect to where the repository went, on the pages,\nover git and over the API, so a clone made yesterday still fetches.\n\nThe ids the forge's own routes occupy (api, git, login, assets and the\nrest) are refused as principal ids, since an owner is the first segment\nof every address; a repository may be called anything a slug allows.\nDeleting a repository asks for its full name.\n\nA forge from before this change adopts the model with\ncairn admin adopt-owners, which renames each repository under its owner\nand moves its directory in one step; serve refuses to start while any\nrepository lacks an owner in its name, and says which command to run.\nThe first-run walk creates under /ada, and the tests address every\nrepository by its owner.\n\nChange-Id: Iowners0097\nSigned-off-by: Mandip Adhikari <92096340+mandipadk@users.noreply.github.com>",
